    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d308">

                <pb facs="0353" n="237" sameAs="frus:frus1914/pg237"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 839.00/1288.</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">Minister Sullivan to
                        the Secretary of State.</hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#center">[Telegram—Extract.]</seg>
                </opener>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">American Legation</hi>, <lb/>
                            <hi rendition="#italic">Santo Domingo</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1914-06-06T18:00:00-04:40">
                            <hi rendition="#italic">June 6, 1914, 6 p.m.</hi>
                        </date>
                    </dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>Government preparing for election on 7th and 8th and claims will proceed without
                    inconvenience in eight of twelve provinces. Minister for Foreign Affairs says
                    that supplementary election will be held when insurrection is subdued. I have
                    made preparations for observation of elections. Government asserts it can not be
                    held responsible for non-participation in the elections by opposing elements who
                    have preferred to seek success by force of arms.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Sullivan</hi></signed>.</closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
